<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tritium Magallum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tritium Magallum was a town of the Berones in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley, on the site of modern Tricio near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najera">Nájera</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-rioja">La Rioja</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. Under Roman rule in the 1st and 2nd centuries CE it was the largest centre producing terra sigillata hispanica, the red-gloss tableware of Roman Spain, exported across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberian Peninsula</a> and beyond.</p></div>
